% decline_struct_diseq_bad.glp — FR-036 DECLINE (NEGATIVE: must be REJECTED at
% load). \= (structural disequality) was deliberately REMOVED from GLP: it is
% ill-defined applied patiently over partial terms (a later bind can falsify a
% committed verdict). A clause using it in guard position must be rejected.
% Canonical GLP form: ~(X? =?= Y?).
exported procedure ddiff(_?, _?, _).
ddiff(X, Y, yes) :- X? \= Y? | true.
